opex.text:
Selling, general and administrative expenses were $99.6 million for the 2026 Quarter, compared to $67.1 million for the 2025 Quarter. The $32.5 million increase was primarily related to:

• an increase in audit and legal expenses of $11.8 million, primarily due to the $11.0 million litigation settlement expense recognized in connection with the Grünenthal Settlement (refer to Note 5, License Agreements );

• an increase in acquisition-related expenses of $5.2 million primarily due to expenses incurred related to the Azstarys Acquisition;

• an increase in salaries, wages and benefits of $9.2 million, primarily due to additional headcount to support the ongoing growth and commercialization of Jornay PM and Azstarys, as well as higher stock-based compensation expense; and

• an increase in sales and marketing expenses of $8.2 million, primarily due to expenses incurred to support Jornay PM and Azstarys.

Gain on fair value remeasurement of contingent consideration was $2.9 million in the 2026 Quarter, compared to less than $0.1 million in the 2025 Quarter. The increase was due to the remeasurement of the contingent consideration associated with the Azstarys Acquisition.

